{
  "about": [
    "The frontmatter privacy corpus: one spec, two classifiers. Rust (crates/frontmatter, tests/corpus.rs) and TS (packages/core/src/markdown/frontmatter-privacy.test.ts) both assert every case.",
    "privacy is public | private | unreadable; reason names why an unreadable block can't be read. A `rust` or `ts` object overrides the expectation for that side only, with `why`: the two YAML parsers (saphyr, yaml) disagree there.",
    "Where the sides disagree on whether the note is withheld at all, `divergence` names the stricter side (rustStricter or tsStricter): each parser accepts some syntax the other rejects, and a block one side can't load is withheld there when it mentions private. Both corpus tests fail on any disagreement a case doesn't pin.",
    "Add a case for any new tricky YAML; fixtures/parity/README.txt explains the divergence classes."
  ],
